        "title": "Add it to your list of places to go",
        "text": "Yes, this temple is very interesting and it is worth paying a few dollars for a guide to tell you all about it.  We saw many cremations of varying economic status.  It was a bit overwhelming at the start, especially when families arrive with the bodies and bring them to the water.  But once you deal with that, it is very interesting and worth a visit.  We got pressured by those \"Lonely Planet\" guys (that's what they called themselves), especially the one with the very long blonde hair and painted faces - they wanted me to give them $20 each!!  Don't succumb to the pressure!  I'm not rich.  I gave them $20 for 6 of them.  For 2 photos, that is more than enough!  Apart from that and pressure from the guide to pay $20 (we had been told by our driver to pay $5!), once you get past that, it is well worth the visit.",
