      {
        "review_id": 183343948,
        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r183343948-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "Hindu cremations and photogenic sadhus",
        "text": "Nepal's equivalent of Varanasi costs an eye-watering 1000Rs to enter (though if you approach from the entrance closer to the Boudha you might get there for free as we didn't see anyone there checking tickets!) Here the cremations of the dead occur on the banks of the holy river. It's very moving moving but you'll need a strong stomach as you may see heads of hair a-blaze! \nUnlike Varanasi, there's no problem taking photos and a cluster of photographers on the opposite bank quickly gather after 9am. \nThe sadhus arrive between 8-9am and gather in a prominent position close to the bridge where they make a healthy living posing for photos. Expect to pay 100Rs. This will buy you as many photos as you like. Its well worth it as they look amazing!",
