      {
        "review_id": 183328378,
        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r183328378-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "It's the only site where I actually hired a guide",
        "text": "I visited here my first day in Katmandu and it's the only site where I actually hired a guide. I had been here 15 years before and had a very dim memory of it. I didn't recall having seen cremations or the many ceremonies for family conducted by priests. I enjoyed taking photos of these scenes and of the temples on the Bagmati river. My guide took me all around including up to the top of the hill and through many of the far flung temple sites. His greatest value was that he showed me the best places to take pictures - many guides won't pick up on what you want to do and will just recite the text that spins in their head. ",
