      {
        "review_id": 182907458,
        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r182907458-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "See to believe",
        "text": "Many who have been to India will find this a familiar site, but the arrangement and intensity here were more extreme than other Hindu temples I'd seen. Please - show some respect and don't snap pictures of the cremations. I know it's hard, but imagine someone showing up at YOUR mother's funeral and putting a camera in your face. NO.  The fee to get in here is around 10 dollars US now, and part of that is discourage too much tourism to the area. If you go in there and act like a jerk, you'll make it more expensive or perhaps one day even forbidden for other curious foreign eyes to experience.\n\nSeriously, go here and behave yourself. Watch out for the overly photo happy 'hermits' volunteering their mugshot for cash. ",
